      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS the full and faithful discharge of the responsibilities vested in the Mayor of the City of New York by the Charter and other laws applicable to his powers and duties will be substantially aided by grouping the various agencies of the City having relation to the health of the people of the City and the care and treatment of the sick, injured, aged and infirm into a manageable system for executive control and review so as to permit the Mayor to communicate more effectively with and exercise leadership over such agencies; and",
